## Frontend architecture

The shared host resolves the correct Parameter Structure and passes the current descriptor, value and context to its registered components.

Do not add application fetching or persistence logic inside the Field/ReadOnly components.

Existing Parameter Structures are reused by Model Forge; this prompt is for implementing a newly generated structure.

## Editable Field contract

The Field receives:

```js
{
  parameter,
  value,
  onChange,
  error,
  disabled,
  parameterContext,
}
```

`value` is the complete current value.

Treat object/array values as immutable.

`onChange(nextValue)` replaces the complete current value.

Do not call it as `(id, value)` unless that pair is literally the canonical parameter value.

Display the supplied `error` when appropriate.

Prevent changes when `disabled` is true.

## ReadOnly contract

The ReadOnly component receives:

```js
{
  parameter,
  value,
  parameterContext,
}
```

It displays the same canonical value without mutation.

